      "level": 2,
      "content": "6.2 Space Technology"
    },
    {
      "id": "4xbynso",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "ISRO's Satish Dhawan Space Centre is in Sriharikota, Andhra Pradesh, but Maharashtra has key ISRO units.",
        "ISRO Space Applications Centre – various units in Maharashtra",
        "Liquid Propulsion Systems Centre – components manufactured here",
        "Vikram Sarabhai Space Centre's unit – test facilities",
        "Pune has IUCAA (Inter-University Centre for Astronomy and Astrophysics) – one of India's premier astronomy research institutes",
        "Giant Metrewave Radio Telescope (GMRT): Located at Khodad near Narayangaon, Pune district. It is the world's largest low-frequency radio telescope array."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "n0856h0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6.3 Nuclear Power Plants in Maharashtra"
    },
    {
      "id": "51v1ym1",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Tarapur Atomic Power Station (TAPS)</strong></p>",
            "<p>Tarapur, Palghar district; India's first nuclear power plant (1969); 4 units; 1400 MW capacity</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Jaitapur Nuclear Power Project</strong></p>",
            "<p>Ratnagiri district (proposed); will be world's largest nuclear power park when completed; French technology (Areva/EDF EPR reactors); 9900 MW planned</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
